<strong>Open plan bathroom renovation</strong> is becoming an increasingly popular choice for homeowners who want to create a hotel-inspired bedroom suite with a greater sense of space and luxury. Instead of separating the bathroom from the bedroom with traditional walls, an open-plan design creates a seamless connection between the two areas, resulting in a brighter, more contemporary living environment.

While the concept looks stunning in luxury homes, an open-plan bathroom requires careful planning. Privacy, ventilation, lighting and storage all need to work together to create a space that's practical as well as beautiful.
<h2>What Is an Open Plan Bathroom?</h2>
An open-plan bathroom is designed without the conventional enclosed layout found in most homes.

Rather than having a fully separate bathroom, features such as freestanding baths, walk-in showers or double vanities are incorporated into the bedroom or connected through partially divided spaces using glass partitions, timber screens or bespoke joinery.

The result is a more spacious and luxurious master suite that feels open while still maintaining clearly defined zones. Reviewing inspiring <a href="https://www.oraanj-interiors.co.uk/luxurious-master-bathroom-ideas-for-your-london-home/">luxurious master bathroom ideas for your London home</a> offers insight into how freestanding tubs and open layouts can be harmoniously styled.
